Step 1 — Open Visual Studio
1. Open Visual Studio 2019.
2. Click:
Create a new project
Step 2 — Select Project
1. Search:
ASP.NET Core Web App

2. Select it.
3. Click Next.
Step 3 — Configure Project
Enter:
Project Name  HelloWebApp
Click Create.

Step 4 — Choose Framework
Select: (Model-View-Controller)
Click Create.     


Step 5 — Display Hello World
Open:
Controllers
   → HomeController.cs

Replace the code with:
using System.Web.Mvc;

namespace HelloWebApp.Controllers
{
    public class HomeController : Controller
    {
        public ActionResult Index()
        {
            return Content("Hello World from ASP.NET MVC!");
        }
    }
}

Save the file.
Step 6 — Run the Application
Press:
F5

Output
Hello World from ASP.NET Core!

Step 7 — Create Simple Form
Open:
Controllers
   → HomeController.cs

Replace the previous code with:
using System.Web.Mvc;

namespace HelloWebApp.Controllers
{
    public class HomeController : Controller
    {
        public ActionResult Index()
        {
            return View();
        }

        [HttpPost]
        public ActionResult Index(string name)
        {
            ViewBag.Message = "Welcome " + name;
            return View();
        }
    }
}

Step 8 — Edit the View
Open:
Views
   → Home
      → Index.cshtml

Replace its contents with:
<form method="post">

    <label>Name:</label>

    <input type="text" name="name" />

    <button type="submit">Submit</button>

</form>

@if (ViewBag.Message != null)
{
    <h2>@ViewBag.Message</h2>
}

Save the file.     
Step 9 — Run the Application
Press:
F5

Enter:
John in the Name field.
Click:
Submit
Output
Welcome John

